# Views

## Framework semantics

CakePHP uses `.php` templates, cells, and helpers under `templates/` / `View/`. Presentation is real framework surface — but **core cakephp-agent skills intentionally do not deep-author view/cell/helper catalogs in v1**.

## Required behavior

- Follow existing project template/layout/helper conventions discovered via `inspect-before-coding`.
- Do not invent Laravel Blade, Livewire, or Twig stacks unless the project already uses them.
- Keep substantial domain/persistence logic out of templates; templates display and submit.
- Cells/helpers are fine when the project already uses them for reusable presentation fragments.

## Anti-patterns

- Inventing Blade / Livewire (not Laravel defaults)
- Fat templates with query/persistence logic
- Rewriting the app’s template system without an explicit request

## Review checklist

- [ ] Template changes match neighboring layouts/elements
- [ ] No new template engine introduced casually
- [ ] Domain rules remain on Tables/validators
